@startuml
!theme plain
title Full-mode UDP and DNS data path

participant "HEV UDP-in-TCP" as HEV
participant "Client association registry" as Registry
participant "SSH relay frame pump" as Pump
participant "relux-relay association registry" as Relay
participant "Exit-host UDP socket" as Socket
participant "Destination or resolver" as Dest

HEV -> Registry : validated IPv4, IPv6, or domain datagram
Registry -> Registry : allocate or reuse active generation association ID
Registry -> Pump : UDP_DATAGRAM within effective limits
alt queue has capacity
  Pump -> Relay : framed bytes over SSH exec stdio
  Relay -> Socket : bounded association socket send
  Socket -> Dest : UDP datagram from user host
  Dest --> Socket : UDP response
  Socket --> Relay : source endpoint plus bytes
  Relay --> Pump : UDP_DATAGRAM response
  Pump --> Registry : association-scoped response
  Registry --> HEV : HEV frame with observed source endpoint
else queue or resource limit reached
  Pump --> Registry : typed drop or bounded error
  Registry --> HEV : documented association-visible outcome
end

group DNS priority without protocol privilege
  HEV -> Registry : tunnel-owned DNS query
  Registry -> Pump : priority class within fixed ceilings
  note right of Pump
  Control remains highest priority.
  DNS cannot bypass byte, time,
  association, or retry ceilings.
  end note
end
@enduml